sam3d upstream-parity exemption for the F32 MMF route.

The sam-3d-objects-ggml upstream carries NO F32 cuBLAS route (their combined
patch leaves mmf.cu at the v0.21.0 base), so every F32 mul_mat in their runs
executes the Ampere TF32 MMF path. Our upstream_accuracy patch routes F32
through cuBLAS for PyTorch equivalence, which broke sam3d conditioning parity
(DINO/PointPatch tokens diverged at ~1%, TF32-mantissa scale). Exempt nodes
named sam3d_* from the F32 cuBLAS route so they keep the base TF32 MMF
behavior and match the upstream reference bit-for-bit; every other task
keeps the PyTorch-equivalent cuBLAS F32 route unchanged.

--- a/src/ggml-cuda/mmf.cu
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/mmf.cu
@@ -1,4 +1,6 @@
 #include "ggml.h"
+#include <cstring>
+
 #include "mmf.cuh"
 #include "mmid.cuh"
 
@@ -131,12 +133,18 @@
 }
 
 bool ggml_cuda_should_use_mmf(enum ggml_type type, int cc, int warp_size, const int64_t * src0_ne,
-        const size_t * src0_nb, const int src1_ncols, bool mul_mat_id) {
+        const size_t * src0_nb, const int src1_ncols, bool mul_mat_id, const char * dst_name) {
     // The Ampere F32 MMF implementation uses tf32.tf32.f32 MMA operands.
     // TF32 truncates the 23-bit F32 mantissa and is not numerically equivalent
     // to PyTorch F32, which is especially visible in World attention GEMMs.
     // Route F32 through the existing cuBLAS F32 path; keep MMF for F16/BF16.
-    if (type == GGML_TYPE_F32) {
+    // sam3d exemption: the sam-3d-objects-ggml reference keeps the base TF32
+    // MMF F32 behavior (its combined patch has no F32 cuBLAS route), so F32
+    // GEMMs inside sam3d graphs (DINO/PointPatch conditioning, SS flow) must
+    // reproduce TF32 operands for upstream parity. Every other task keeps the
+    // PyTorch-equivalent cuBLAS F32 route.
+    const bool sam3d_f32 = dst_name && strncmp(dst_name, "sam3d_", 6) == 0;
+    if (type == GGML_TYPE_F32 && !sam3d_f32) {
         return false;
     }
     if (ggml_is_quantized(type)) {
